<title>USA: Alanco CEO resigns, chairman takes job.</title>
<headline>Alanco CEO resigns, chairman takes job.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTSDALE, Ariz. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alanco Environmental Resources Corp said on Tuesday its board accepted the resignation of Norman Meyer as chief executive and president and that Chairman Dennis Schlegel would take on the additional role as CEO.</p>
<p>&quot;We appreciate Norm Meyer's service to Alanco,&quot; Schlegel said. &quot;The company came a long way under his leadership and we look forward to building on his achievements.&quot;</p>
<p>Schlegel was named chairman in 1996.</p>
<p>The board also named Ed Maley as acting president of Alanco. Maley has been president of Alanco unit Fry Guy Inc and would continue to hold that job as well, Alanco said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
